// NUMERIC CONTRACT v0.2
All RuleState numbers must be finite JS safe integers unless explicitly encoded fixed-point.
age,maxAge,actionTimeCost,outcomeTimeDelta = integer years >=0.
attributes = integers; injury/丹毒 stacks = integers 0..3.
relation.affinity/trust = integer -100..100; debt = integer -3..3.
probability/multipliers = basis points (0..10000 = 0..100% or 1.0 multiplier); clamp where contract says.
No hidden float accumulation.
Generic roundHalfUpPositive(n,d)=floor((n + floor(d/2))/d), n>=0,d>0.
Time formula may multiply integer baseYears by bps modifiers; round once at final years boundary; min positive action cost=1.
For rulesVersion 2.0.0 authoritative action costs are cultivate=3, travel=2, worldly=1, pursuit=1 years; they are Core-owned versioned safe integers.
Checks compare scaled integers; do not round weighted attribute terms mid-formula, except A08 CheckSpec signed secondary contribution explicitly finalized by event.ref using sign(value)*roundHalfUpPositive(abs(value)*bps,10000) before finalScore.
Reject NaN/Infinity/unsafe integers before reduce.
